	(text "Pin n of J601 / J602 (carrier top side, sockets) mates with pin n of J701 / J702 (upper board, headers).\nThe headers go on the BOTTOM side of the upper board, same rotation as the sockets: KiCad numbers the\nsocket footprint mirrored to the header, so the flipped header lands pin 1 on pin 1.\nSMD socket (top 8.9 mm above its board) + through-hole header (2.5 mm base) on M2.5 x 12 mm spacers:\nthe spacers set the 12.0 mm gap, the connectors stay 0.6 mm short of bottoming out."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 50.8 12.7 0)
